From 4d7040b602402af14bafe87a7fa73c71f352df06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marie-222 <289302950+marie-222@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:48:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] desktop-shell: do not animate input panels in rdprail-shell

show_input_panel_surface() slides the panel in from below, with a spring that
overshoots. With RAIL every step moves a real window on the client, so the
candidate window of an input method slid in and bounced at its final position
each time it was shown. Skip the animation when the shell runs with the rdprail
API; the behaviour of desktop-shell is unchanged.
---
 desktop-shell/input-panel.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/desktop-shell/input-panel.c b/desktop-shell/input-panel.c
index ba910126..76be598a 100644
--- a/desktop-shell/input-panel.c
+++ b/desktop-shell/input-panel.c
@@ -114,6 +114,11 @@ show_input_panel_surface(struct input_panel_surface *ipsurf)
 		break;
 	}
 
+	/* In rdprail-shell, every step of the animation moves a real window on the client (it slides in
+	 * from below and bounces at the final position each time the panel is shown): do not animate. */
+	if (shell->rdprail_api)
+		return;
+
 	if (ipsurf->anim)
 		weston_view_animation_destroy(ipsurf->anim);
 
